WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:01.601
This is quite something to see.

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.004
A tweet from the Canadian prime minister

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:08.141
saying that he ordered this object

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:12.445
to be taken down over Canadian skies.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.147
What more can you tell us?

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.149
It also speaks, in fact,

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:17.283
to the seriousness

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.251
of what's happened here

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:19.619
and the chain of command

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.454
and I will note that in his tweet,

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:22.856
the prime minister also indicated,

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:23.523
of course,

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.858
this is close coordination

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:25.959
with the White House

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.861
and with President Joe Biden.

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.963
At issue here,

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:30.930
Jim, is really

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.832
what is going on with these objects

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.434
and the threat that they pose.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.002
Now, remember

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:36.903
that they would have been

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.505
given some kind of intelligence

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:39.272
when Nord

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:40.573
had actually spotted

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:42.308
this high altitude object,

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:43.410
as they're calling it,

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.477
to give an indication

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.780
that possibly there was a threat.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.248
I would assume that if it was over

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.315
northern Canada,

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:50.817
that Canadian forces,

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.252
the Air Force, would have determined

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:54.120
that they could shoot it down

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.089
without a risk to people on the ground.

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:57.524
And more than that,

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:57.857
the prime

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.025
minister is now saying

00:00:59.025 --> 00:00:59.959
the Canadian Forces

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.961
will lead the recovery effort again

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.364
to ascertain exactly what this is.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:06.332
Does it pose a threat?

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:08.268
And who it belongs to?

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:09.969
Because remember, in the last objects

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:11.204
you were just talking to Natasha

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:13.206
about that second one, still a mystery.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.542
Obviously, this a mystery as well.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.243
What is it?

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.979
Why does it continue to enter both U.S.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:22.315
and Canadian airspace?

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:25.285
And what can Canadian forces and the U.S.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.120
now learn from having shot it down

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.888
and trying to recover the debris?

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.457
We don't have any more details yet.

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:31.891
We have reached out to the Canadian

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.393
Defense Ministry to understand

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.561
what kind of a recovery

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.762
operation is underway

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:38.364
and how complicated that might be.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.500
But given the way the close coordination

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.068
has been happening between the U.S.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.170
and Canada, remember

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:44.838
through Nora,

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:45.138
they're all

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.372
looking at the same intelligence

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:47.707
in terms of what is it?

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:48.975
Does it pose a threat?

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.276
They now need to determine

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.579
exactly what to do going forward.

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:53.813
At issue, though, Jim,

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.081
the most important thing is

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.182
you've lost two objects.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.217
Who do they belong to

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:58.651
and why are they entering

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.220
both Canadian and American airspace?

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:02.755
And according to these tweets

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.858
from the Canadian prime minister,

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:07.260
Paula, Canadian forces will now recover

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.829
and analyze the wreckage of this object.

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:11.131
The prime minister

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:13.566
seems to have some degree of confidence

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.468
that there is wreckage

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.937
that is retrievable, recoverable,

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.939
at this point and

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:22.342
possibly available for analysis once

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:24.010
once it's all picked up.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.745
That's interesting as well.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:27.013
It is very interesting.

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:27.847
And obviously, as I said,

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:28.615
first and foremost,

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:29.482
they want to make sure

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:30.316
that assuming that down

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.584
there was no risk to anyone

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:32.285
on the ground.

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:32.986
But again,

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:35.655
the recovery efforts, what do they entail

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:36.356
given?

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:37.590
I'd imagine

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.759
you know, in terms of recovery,

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.562
what kind of debris field

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:43.329
are they looking at?

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.564
Again, it did not come down

00:02:44.564 --> 00:02:45.832
as far as we know, in the water

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:46.866
that will make things

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.334
a little bit easier.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.502
Again, they recover

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.770
that second high

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.772
altitude object

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.541
and they'll be in close coordination

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:55.975
with U.S. forces on that

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.378
Just to remind everyone, it

00:02:58.378 --> 00:03:00.180
was actually just yesterday, on Friday

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.281
that Canada's defense

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:03.550
minister, Anita Anand, met with Secretary

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:07.287
Austin to discuss these issues.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.555
And, you know,

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:09.122
President Biden

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:12.025
is expected to visit Canada in March.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:13.793
You know, one of the key issues

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.762
that was already on the agenda, Jim,

00:03:15.762 --> 00:03:17.564
before these objects started

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:18.531
appearing over U.S.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.599
and Canadian airspace

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.768
was Arctic security.

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:23.636
Some of it is certainly menacing

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:24.404
from the point of view

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.139
about what Russia has been going on.

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:27.240
Has been had going on

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.474
in the Arctic region,

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.910
but obviously also China.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.011
And given

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.146
these kinds of threats,

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:35.448
just poking their way into the airspace

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.150
this whole conversation

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.052
about Arctic security over both Canada

00:03:39.052 --> 00:03:39.819
and the United States

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:42.755
will take on a very heightened urgency.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:43.489
And again,

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:44.924
they are looking for a completely

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:47.227
new security architecture here

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:48.061
for the Arctic

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.829
and for the north over both countries.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.331
And this will certainly feature.

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:54.133
You're absolutely right about that.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.468
That's a very good point, Paula.

00:03:55.468 --> 00:03:56.469
I remember from my days

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:57.303
covering the White House

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.439
that both administrations I covered

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:00.273
were becoming

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.507
increasingly concerned

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:02.642
about what was taking place

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:03.610
in the Arctic,

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:04.711
in part

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:05.612
because of the warming

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.380
that is going on up there,

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.349
but also because of the potential

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:11.050
for things like this.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:12.619
Paula Newton,

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:14.020
thank you very much for your time.

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:14.821
Please come back to us

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.122
if you have any new information.

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.156
We'll take it

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.091
just as soon as you have it.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.692
We appreciate it very much.

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:20.560
Joining us now

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.261
to discuss

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:23.196
this further is CNN transportation

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:25.732
analyst Mary Schiavo.

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.934
Mary is a former inspector general

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.769
for the Department of Transportation.

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:32.672
Mary, we were talking to you last weekend

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:35.808
about how weird it was to have a balloon,

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:37.076
a Chinese spy balloon

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:38.611
flying over the United States

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.980
and being shot down off the coast of

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:41.814
South Carolina.

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.116
And then lo and behold, here

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:44.717
we are one week later,

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.119
we had the incident that took place

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:47.654
in Alaska yesterday.

00:04:47.654 --> 00:04:49.455
And then we don't even know

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:50.223
a whole lot about

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:51.791
what is taking place today.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:53.092
The Canadian prime minister

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:54.794
ordering the takedown

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:57.096
of an unidentified object over the Yukon.

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:59.465
That is very strange.

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:02.201
Well, very strange,

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:02.702
but I've

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:03.836
been working in Alaska

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:04.671
for two and a half weeks

00:05:04.671 --> 00:05:07.040
on a different airplane crash case.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.274
The the difference

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:08.508
in the

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:11.511
activity here with military aviation.

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:14.314
I'm literally I can see it

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:15.114
you know, aviation,

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:16.316
an air base from here.

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:18.151
There are AWACS planes,

00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:20.420
you know, the airborne early surveillance

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:21.554
radar planes

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:22.655
from the military base

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:24.324
circling around Alaska.

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:26.159
I mean, there's a tremendous increase

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:27.093
in activity here

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.761
just on surveillance activities

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:30.229
from from,

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:31.631
you know, fixed wing aircraft

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:32.865
and the AWACS

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:34.734
and the important thing to note

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.135
is the United States.

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:36.869
And, of course,

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:38.504
Canada has every right

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.840
to take these aircraft down

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.775
or wherever these objects are.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:43.843
Balloons

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:45.411
because we have a series of treaties

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:46.846
with all nations of the world.

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:48.247
And we also have requirements

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.215
for aircraft

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:50.416
to identify themselves,

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:51.217
to be identified,

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:53.586
particularly at the altitudes

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:54.687
at which they're flying.

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:55.521
Yes, you can do

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:56.989
what's called visual flight.

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:57.724
You don't have to have

00:05:57.724 --> 00:05:59.559
a transponder on board.

00:05:59.559 --> 00:06:00.526
But at the altitudes

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:01.861
that some of these objects have been,

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:04.030
they will interfere with traffic,

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.531
with commercial air traffic.

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.767
I mean, some planes can fly at 40,000

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:09.268
50,000 feet.

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:11.003
And by not identifying what

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:11.938
the object is,

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:13.940
military aircraft can fly up to you.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:15.608
Even if that's happened to me

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:16.709
when I was in flight school,

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.344
they can fly up to a civilian aircraft

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:19.846
and ask you to identify yourself

00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:20.680
if you're too close

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.515
to military installations.

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:23.349
And Alaska

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:25.351
is full of military installations.

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:27.820
So I think the heightened surveillance

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:30.523
up here, in addition to realizing

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:31.624
there is something there

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:33.760
that the nations need to find out,

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.762
they're within their rights to do it now.

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:39.098
And you're absolutely right about that

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:39.966
in terms of the danger

00:06:39.966 --> 00:06:41.267
to civilian aircraft,

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:43.202
because as we were discussing

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:44.203
about what took place

00:06:44.203 --> 00:06:45.104
in Alaska yesterday,

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:46.239
that was the concern

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:48.841
that that unidentified object was

00:06:49.809 --> 00:06:51.477
hovering around 40,000 feet.

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:52.578
That puts it at risk.

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.747
For colliding with civilian aircraft.

00:06:55.214 --> 00:06:57.817
That makes it a huge

00:06:57.817 --> 00:07:00.953
aviation security priority.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:02.121
That's right. In the skies up here.

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:03.556
We're very busy yesterday,

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:04.190
not you know,

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:04.924
it's always busy

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:06.759
with civilian aircraft in Alaska

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:08.528
because that's a way of life.

00:07:08.528 --> 00:07:10.563
But there was a lot of military presence

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.698
in the skies yesterday over Anchorage.

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:13.866
And environs.

00:07:13.866 --> 00:07:14.967
And, you know,

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:16.135
are they just picking up more

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:17.837
now that everyone's paying attention?

00:07:17.837 --> 00:07:19.005
Well, really, no,

00:07:19.005 --> 00:07:20.072
because over the years

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:21.240
there have been many sightings

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.108
of various things.

00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:23.910
But a lot of times

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:24.744
the government didn't

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:25.912
pay much attention to them.

00:07:25.912 --> 00:07:26.846
And when I was inspector

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:27.980
general, the DOD,

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.749
obviously the FAA was underresourced

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:31.083
and there would be lots of reports.

00:07:31.083 --> 00:07:33.019
Oh, the FAA is hiding

00:07:33.019 --> 00:07:34.020
you know, is covering up.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.788
Brown identified flying objects.

00:07:35.788 --> 00:07:37.757
Now, when we investigated,

00:07:37.757 --> 00:07:40.126
they always had an earthly origin.

00:07:40.893 --> 00:07:43.162
But now with heightened attention,

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:44.897
I think probably more will be found

00:07:44.897 --> 00:07:46.933
because that's generally how it works.

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:49.168
When you pay attention, you find more.

00:07:49.502 --> 00:07:51.671
But they always have an origin

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:54.173
at least so far here on Earth.

00:07:55.708 --> 00:07:56.175
Yes.

00:07:56.175 --> 00:07:58.211
And let me ask you about

00:07:58.211 --> 00:07:59.846
what was reported about Alaska

00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:02.849
in that the object that was taken down

00:08:02.849 --> 00:08:04.383
yesterday was described as being

00:08:04.383 --> 00:08:06.752
about the size of a small car.

00:08:06.752 --> 00:08:09.121
Does that sound like another balloon type

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:10.256
aircraft to you

00:08:10.256 --> 00:08:13.459
or does that sound like a drone?

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:15.962
Well, there were some reports on pilots.

00:08:16.128 --> 00:08:17.263
The pilots who went up

00:08:17.263 --> 00:08:18.097
take a look at it

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:19.499
themselves, had mixed reports.

00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:20.566
Some thought balloon

00:08:20.566 --> 00:08:22.969
and some that it was a drone.

00:08:23.202 --> 00:08:25.171
And, of course, you know, drones,

00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:25.471
you know,

00:08:25.471 --> 00:08:27.206
they look very different nowadays.

00:08:27.206 --> 00:08:29.075
They don't look like aircraft of years

00:08:29.075 --> 00:08:29.809
gone by.

00:08:29.809 --> 00:08:31.410
So I think we'll have to wait

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:32.745
on the government to tell that.

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:33.946
But without a doubt,

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:35.915
the balloon that they got,

00:08:35.915 --> 00:08:37.950
they now say, was doing

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.485
communications surveillance.

00:08:39.485 --> 00:08:40.920
Which one would you know,

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.021
expect a balloon?

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:43.589
If you've got a satellite

00:08:43.589 --> 00:08:44.790
to take pictures,

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:45.791
a balloon surveillance

00:08:45.791 --> 00:08:46.325
would have to be

00:08:46.325 --> 00:08:47.660
